# fstab — Orange Pi 4 LTS (Rockchip RK3399 arm64) light desktop.
#
# The boot media varies by flavor. This board boots from microSD or its onboard
# 16GB eMMC. There is NO M.2/NVMe slot on the Orange Pi 4 LTS — unlike the
# Orange Pi 5 Plus this file was forked from (see specs-orangepi4-lts/README.md).
# Like the Frite builder, this image produces LIVE/INSTALLER ISO media + a stage4
# tarball — there is NO build_img/.img assembly step here. The LIVE flavor boots
# a squashfs root ephemerally (this fstab is largely inert there; / is the live
# overlay). The INSTALLER flavor (install-orangepi4-lts.sh) partitions the target
# medium AT INSTALL TIME and rewrites the LABEL=/PARTUUID device columns below
# for the medium it actually wrote, so the installed system mounts the right
# partitions. The placeholder device paths below are replaced at install time;
# do not rely on them literally.
#
# <device>            <mount>  <type>   <options>                              <dump> <pass>
LABEL=OPI4L_BOOT     /boot    vfat     defaults,noatime,nosuid,nodev,noexec   0      2
LABEL=OPI4L_ROOT     /        ext4     defaults,noatime                       0      1
tmpfs               /tmp     tmpfs    defaults,nosuid,nodev,noexec,size=256m 0      0
tmpfs               /run     tmpfs    defaults,nosuid,nodev,mode=0755        0      0

# No zram helper here (unlike the Frite 512MB SKU): the Orange Pi 4 LTS ships
# 4GB of LPDDR4, so a swap helper is not baked by default. Add one
# post-first-boot if a workload needs it. Note this is the LOW end of the range
# the Orange Pi 5 fork assumed (4/8/16/32GB) — 4GB is all there is here.
